FATAL_OBJECTIONS:
- Bordt 2410.03249 MIS-CITATION: novelty_killer VERIFIED via arXiv that Bordt is about whether contaminated examples are FORGOTTEN at scale, NOT about applying n-gram decontam and calling removal benign. The packet's entire novelty pivot ("Bordt saw removal, called it benign; our delta = it's NOT benign") rests on a paper that says no such thing. This is not a minor citation error — it is the LOAD-BEARING novelty anchor collapsing. Must be repaired before any GREEN.
- PRIOR-ART SWEEP INCOMPLETE: novelty_killer could not complete a ≥2-independent-source collision sweep (egress blocked). Per committee rules, GREEN requires adequate prior-art search. Not met.
- IID BERNOULLI ASSUMPTION UNVALIDATED: evaluation_prosecutor and theory_skeptic independently flag that modeling k-gram matches as independent Bernoulli(q) events overstates length-dependent removal in real text where n-gram overlaps are bursty/correlated (contiguous phrase copying, templates, boilerplate). The union-bound is an UPPER bound under IID; real removal-vs-length curve could be substantially flatter, shrinking Delta proportionally. No evidence presented that the IID model approximates real corpus behavior.

REQUIRED_EVIDENCE:
- [L1-CRITICAL] Real-benchmark removal curve: apply 8-gram and 13-gram decontam to GSM8K/QuALITY/MMLU test sets against a real web corpus (C4/Pile/FineWeb). Plot empirical removal probability vs item length. If the curve is substantially flatter than 1-(1-q)^(L-k+1), the IID model overstates the effect and the headline magnitude is wrong.
- [L1-CRITICAL] Measured real length<->difficulty slope: compute per-item accuracy from a production model (Llama-3, GPT-4) on GSM8K/MMLU and regress against item length to obtain an empirical alpha. Without this, "+0.9-1.7pt" is a simulation artifact of chosen alpha, not a finding (theory_skeptic).
- [L1-CRITICAL] Realized score inflation: using the real removal set and real per-item accuracies, compute the actual Delta on at least one benchmark where alpha is empirically confirmed >0.
- [NOVELTY-CRITICAL] Complete prior-art sweep on "decontamination false positives / over-removal / length bias / selection bias in benchmark filtering" with ≥2 independent sources per collision candidate. Specifically search for any work that frames removal as a length-correlated or difficulty-correlated estimand bias (not just "significant filtering").
- [NOVELTY-CRITICAL] Replace Bordt 2410.03249 anchor with the CORRECT sources: GPT-3 (2005.14165 Appendix C) and Llama-3 (2407.21783) both report large benign-treated removal fractions and re-score on "clean subsets." The novelty delta must be measured against THESE — "they treated removal as benign collateral; we show it isn't when alpha>0."

MANDATORY_BASELINES:
- Real corpus n-gram overlap vs IID Bernoulli: measure actual per-k-gram match correlation structure in (benchmark, web corpus) pairs to validate or refute the independence assumption (evaluation_prosecutor).
- Length-independent null model: compare union-bound fit (MAE=0.012) against a constant removal-rate baseline to demonstrate the length-dependent model specifically fits better, not just "fits okay" (theory_skeptic).
- Per-benchmark alpha measurement: empirical length<->difficulty slope on GSM8K, MMLU, QuALITY from published per-item accuracies — this is the ONLY thing that converts the structural shift into score inflation.

